Let's avoid jshint comments. I assume this is failing because of unused. We could, instead, use a var module.
@timmywil, you're right about the unused. Could you clarify what you meant by "a var module"? I am really curious.
A variable will get moved to a module if another module needs it. We have a custom build system that compiles modules containing single return statements into var statements.

``` js
// File foo.js
define(function() {
  return 'awesome';
});
```

becomes...

``` js
var foo = 'awesome';
```

This allows multiple modules to share the same variable without affecting the built file size. It also limits the scope of variables to the modules that use them, bypassing the need for `unused` workarounds.
Ah, that's cool. Thank you for explaining.
